.workspace/

# The redaction model's response cache. `redact_media.py propose` writes it
# INSIDE the media directory it is reviewing, which is a directory whose whole
# purpose is to be committed - so a `git add fixtures/demo-01/media` would have
# swept up the model's raw output, including its proposed boxes over faces and
# plates, alongside the images those boxes describe. Ignored rather than moved,
# because the cache belongs beside the media it was computed from; what it does
# not belong in is a commit.
.redact-cache/
